      "description": "Egyptian semolina cake soaked in sugar syrup",
      "seasonings": [
        "vanilla"
      ],
      "ingredients": [
        "2 cups shredded coconut",
        "2 cups semolina",
        "1 cup sugar",
        "1 cup yogurt",
        "1 tbsp baking powder",
        "For syrup: 2 cups sugar, 1 cup water, 1 tbsp lemon juice",
        "Whole cloves",
        "Almond slivers"
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Mix coconut, semolina, sugar, yogurt, baking powder",
        "Spread in greased pan 1/2-inch thick",
        "Cut into diamonds or squares",
        "Place almond in center of each piece",
        "Press clove on top",
        "Bake at 350°F for 30-35 minutes until golden",
        "Meanwhile, heat sugar and water for syrup, add lemon juice",
        "Pour hot syrup over hot cake",
        "Cool completely"
      ],
      "notes": "Must pour hot syrup on hot cake",
      "fun_fact": "Basboosa is a staple at Egyptian celebrations and holidays",
      "alternatives": [
        "All almond instead of coconut",
